            {
                "entry_id": "bb0cf36a-1fd3-3fea-b2a3-9761597af304",
                "word": "marge",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "39ca3824-e539-4f30-a545-56e43b7b6a98",
                        "entry_id": "bb0cf36a-1fd3-3fea-b2a3-9761597af304",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "marges"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1ecb685-0a1e-34b7-90bb-55b52e341aac",
                        "entry_id": "bb0cf36a-1fd3-3fea-b2a3-9761597af304",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Margin; edge; brink or verge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "948671df-a36b-4a72-a58b-da2cc9b618b5",
                                "sense_id": "b1ecb685-0a1e-34b7-90bb-55b52e341aac",
                                "text": "[…] And thy sea-marge, sterile and rocky-hard, / Where thou thyself dost air [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12706c32-0bd1-4583-b89a-2ea3fd29c9de",
                                "sense_id": "b1ecb685-0a1e-34b7-90bb-55b52e341aac",
                                "text": "[F]lowers that in perennial blow / Round the moist marge of Persian fountains cling; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36a4aea7-3d7f-48f9-a49f-d0fa07a4a294",
                                "sense_id": "b1ecb685-0a1e-34b7-90bb-55b52e341aac",
                                "text": "So be it: there no shade can last / ⁠In that deep dawn behind the tomb, / ⁠But clear from marge to marge shall bloom / The eternal landscape of the past; / A lifelong tract of time reveal'd; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f10ba004-da36-411f-a702-4a1b1f2656c5",
                                "sense_id": "b1ecb685-0a1e-34b7-90bb-55b52e341aac",
                                "text": "Upon an easy slope it lies at large, / And scarcely overlaps the long curved crest / Which swells out two leagues from the river marge, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "219b7755-47b6-4dc7-8a43-69315620d7d5",
                                "sense_id": "b1ecb685-0a1e-34b7-90bb-55b52e341aac",
                                "text": "Till I came to the marge of Lake Lebarge, and a derelict there lay; / It was jammed in the ice, but I saw in a trice it was called the \"Alice May.\" / And I looked at it, and I thought a bit, and I looked at my frozen chum: / Then \"Here,\" said I, with a sudden cry, \"is my cre-ma-tor-eum.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
